  "notes": "2-in/2-out USB interface, 24 bit / 192 kHz, USB bus-powered (5 V, min. 500 mA). Ports and controls follow the manual, chapter 'Connections and controls'. CH1/CH2: XLR/6.35 mm combo (mic, line, instrument), 48 V phantom via the PHAN slider. PHONE I/O: 3.5 mm 4-pin jack for a smartphone; the phone's audio is played through the interface, the interface's inputs are sent to the phone. Modelling assumptions, not stated in the manual: MONITORING fully to DIRECT means no DAW playback on the outputs, fully to DAW means no direct signal; MONO puts CH1 and CH2 on both main outputs, STEREO puts CH1 left and CH2 right; MAIN OUTPUT and PHONES volume at MIN are treated as silent; the phone's audio goes to the main outputs and the headphones. The manual lists HI-Z once; the product page says each channel has one - shown here as one switch until checked on the device. Start positions (STEREO, PHAN off, HI-Z off, knobs in the middle) are app defaults, not a factory setting.",
